# Rottenmouth Viper's ability once triggered is independent of it (CR 113.7a). On turn 3 it attacks with one blight counter,
# and Bot2 exiles it with Swords to Plowshares in response (Bot1 gains 6). The ability puts no counter on it, since it is
# no longer on the battlefield, and counts the one counter it had as it last existed there (CR 608.2h): Bot2 answers once,
# losing 4 life (16 after the first time, 12 now). The attack's damage is gone with it.

[Bot1 Deck]
Island
Black Lotus
Show and Tell
Rottenmouth Viper
Island x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Plains
Swords to Plowshares x15

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot1.Hand.Show and Tell.Cast
Bot1.Choose(Rottenmouth Viper)
Bot2.Choose()
Bot2.Modes(Lose 4 life)
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Plains.Play
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Attack(Rottenmouth Viper > Bot2)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Swords to Plowshares.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Rottenmouth Viper)
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
? Exile = Rottenmouth Viper
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot2.Modes(Lose 4 life)
! Bot2.Modes

[Expect]
Turn = 3
Bot1.Life = 26
Bot2.Life = 12
Exile = Rottenmouth Viper
